/*
 * Shared test fixture — not shipped in any package.
 *
 * Ground truth for data/ships/engineering-options.jsonc — which blueprints and experimental
 * effects appear in each stock module's ordinary engineering menu. Availability is per module,
 * not per blueprint: `groups` pins every group's menu by content, `modules` that a module resolves
 * to its group, `exclusions` the modules
 * that take their group's blueprints but not all of its experimental effects (a small
 * Multi-cannon cannot take Phasing Sequence), and
 * `blueprintUnion` that a blueprint-level query returns the union across every group offering it.
 * `splitFamilies` pins the families upstream splits in two by denying blueprints per module — a
 * Guardian Power Plant and an ordinary one are the same kind of module with different menus, so
 * they are different groups, and only the ordinary half has an experimental slot.
 * `antiGuardianZoneResistance` pins the whole of that: the recipe that is a Guardian module's
 * entire menu, offered by nine groups, none of which offers an experimental effect. `groupSizes`
 * pins how many modules each group holds, so a module moving between groups fails a test rather
 * than balancing out against the totals; `modules` pins one member of every group by name.
 * `corpus` measures the catalogue against the 181-build community corpus in `builds/`.
 */
