    ]
  },
  "corpus": {
    "description": "The catalogue measured against `fixtures/ships/builds/`. `declaredEngineering` is the corpus total; `ungroupedEntries` counts declarations on modules this catalogue does not group. `blueprintAliases` are recipes reachable under more than one current spelling: each is a family's generic id, where the catalogue lists the family-specific spelling and a build declaring the generic one is engineering the same thing. Anti-Guardian Zone Resistance is not among them — the nine groups offering it list `GuardianModule_Sturdy`, the only spelling of it a journal has been observed to write and the only one the catalogue keys. `journalSpellingsAccepted` counts declarations resolved against the blueprint journal-name collision catalogue rather than by signature — one journal id, two recipes, and only the fitted module says which. 70 of the 71 are `Weapon_Overcharged` on a multi-cannon, which rolls the `MC_Overcharged` the multi-cannon menu lists rather than the recipe every other weapon takes under that id; the 71st spells a wake scanner's Long Range `Sensor_LongRange`, the id the game writes for the sensor suite's different recipe of the same name. `finalPreEngineered` pins the 18 Guardian-weapon, six Expanded Cargo Rack, and one Long Range Abrasion Blaster entries that identify fixed reward articles rather than recipes a player may apply. `notEngineerable` pins only declarations that upstream denies to both the stock module and any separately catalogued article: two Efficient Mk II Plasma Shock Accelerators.",
